---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';

// Owns both "bionic reading online" and "bionic text converter":
// /bionic-reading-converter 308s here (vercel.json).
const pageTitle = "Bionic Reading Online: Free Converter & Reader | BriskRead";
const pageDescription = "Free bionic reading tool: paste text to bold word beginnings and copy it anywhere, or read in bionic mode in the speed reader. Runs in your browser.";
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class="tool-seo mt-8">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <div class="glass content-card">
        <h1>Bionic Reading Online: Free Converter &amp; Reader</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Paste text below and it converts instantly. Each word gets its opening letters bolded, which gives your eye an anchor to land on. Copy the result into a doc, or read it in BriskRead's bionic mode. Everything runs in your browser; nothing is uploaded.
        </p>

        <div class="converter mt-6" id="converter">
          <label for="bionic-input">Your text</label>
          <textarea id="bionic-input" rows="7" placeholder="Paste an article, an email, a chapter…"></textarea>

          <div class="converter-controls mt-4">
            <label for="bionic-strength">Fixation strength: <output id="bionic-strength-out">Medium</output></label>
            <input type="range" id="bionic-strength" min="1" max="3" step="1" value="2" />
            <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="bionic-copy" type="button">Copy result</button>
          </div>

          <h2 class="mt-6">Converted text</h2>
          <div id="bionic-output" class="bionic-output" aria-live="polite"></div>
          <p class="muted mt-2" id="bionic-count">0 words</p>

          <a href="/#importer-card" class="btn btn-primary mt-4">Read it in bionic mode instead</a>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-8">How to read in bionic mode on BriskRead</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Open the <a href="/">BriskRead speed reader</a> and paste text, upload a PDF/EPUB/TXT, or extract a URL.</li>
          <li>Start reading, then switch to <strong>Bionic Mode</strong> in the reader toolbar.</li>
          <li>Optional: turn on Audio Sync for dual-channel focus, or use RSVP mode for single-word flashing.</li>
          <li>Adjust theme (light, sepia, dark, AMOLED) and font size for long sessions.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Does bionic reading work?</h2>
        <p>
          Bionic-style formatting bolds the first part of each word: short words get one bolded letter, longer words get more. The claim is that your brain completes the word from the bolded prefix. Studies have not shown a reliable speed gain, but many readers say the page is easier to keep their place on, which matters more for a long backlog than raw WPM. Treat it as a comfort option and test it on your own reading.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-8">When bionic reading helps</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Long articles</strong>: scan research blogs and news without losing the thread.</li>
          <li><strong>Study notes</strong>: review dense paragraphs you will re-read.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility preference</strong>: some readers prefer bold anchors over pure RSVP flashes.</li>
          <li><strong>Mixed sessions</strong>: switch between bionic page view and RSVP without re-uploading.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Fixation strength</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Light</strong>: roughly a third of each word. Least visually noisy, good for long sessions.</li>
          <li><strong>Medium</strong>: about half. The default, and closest to what most bionic tools produce.</li>
          <li><strong>Heavy</strong>: around two thirds. Strongest anchor, but the contrast between bold and plain drops.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Convert, or just read?</h2>
        <p>
          Convert when the text is going somewhere else: a document you'll print, a passage you're studying, notes you want to re-read. If you just want to get through the text now, open it in the <a href="/">reader</a>, where Bionic is one of six modes and you can pair it with pacing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Bionic reading vs RSVP</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Bionic reading</strong> keeps a full paragraph layout and bolds word prefixes. <strong>RSVP</strong> flashes one word at a fixed point with an Optimal Recognition Point (ORP) highlight. BriskRead includes both, plus Focus, Flow and Page modes and synced text-to-speech, all processed in your browser.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The converter is plain JavaScript running on this page. Your text never leaves the browser, there is no upload, and closing the tab discards it. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="related mt-8">
          <h2>Related free tools</h2>
          <p>
            <a href="/">Online speed reader</a> ·
            <a href="/rsvp-reader">RSVP reader</a> ·
            <a href="/reading-speed-test">Reading speed test</a> ·
            <a href="/pdf-to-speech">PDF to speech</a> ·
            <a href="/extension">Chrome extension</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            Guide: <a href="/blog/how-to-speed-read-online">How to speed read online</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ads-section mt-8">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <AdSlot placement="MID" format="auto" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const input = document.getElementById('bionic-input');
    const output = document.getElementById('bionic-output');
    const count = document.getElementById('bionic-count');
    const strength = document.getElementById('bionic-strength');
    const strengthOut = document.getElementById('bionic-strength-out');
    const copyBtn = document.getElementById('bionic-copy');
    const LABELS = { 1: 'Light', 2: 'Medium', 3: 'Heavy' };
    const RATIOS = { 1: 0.34, 2: 0.5, 3: 0.66 };

    const SAMPLE =
      'Reading a long article is mostly a problem of attention, not of eyesight. ' +
      'Bolding the opening letters of each word gives your eye a fixed place to land, ' +
      'so it stops drifting back over text it has already covered.';

    const WORD = "A-Za-zÀ-ɏ'";
    const esc = (s) => s.replace(/[&<>]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;' })[c]);

    // Walk words and the gaps between them in one pass. Words are letters only,
    // so they need no escaping; everything else does. Escaping the whole string
    // up front instead would turn "&lt;" into text the word regex then bolds.
    const convert = (text, ratio) =>
      text.replace(new RegExp(`([${WORD}]+)|([^${WORD}]+)`, 'g'), (_, word, gap) => {
        if (!word) return esc(gap);
        const cut = Math.max(1, Math.round(word.length * ratio));
        return `<strong>${word.slice(0, cut)}</strong>${word.slice(cut)}`;
      });

    const wordCount = (text) => (text.trim() ? text.trim().split(/\s+/).length : 0);

    const render = () => {
      const ratio = RATIOS[strength.value];
      strengthOut.textContent = LABELS[strength.value];
      const text = input.value || SAMPLE;
      output.innerHTML = convert(text, ratio).replace(/\n/g, '<br />');
      count.textContent = `${wordCount(text)} words${input.value ? '' : ' (sample text)'}`;
    };

    input.addEventListener('input', render);
    strength.addEventListener('input', render);

    copyBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try {
        // Copy rich text so the bolding survives a paste into a doc; plain text
        // is the fallback item so terminals and code editors still get something.
        const html = new Blob([output.innerHTML], { type: 'text/html' });
        const plain = new Blob([output.innerText], { type: 'text/plain' });
        await navigator.clipboard.write([new ClipboardItem({ 'text/html': html, 'text/plain': plain })]);
        copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied';
      } catch {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.innerText).catch(() => {});
        copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied as plain text';
      }
      setTimeout(() => { copyBtn.textContent = 'Copy result'; }, 1800);
    });

    render();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .max-w-3xl { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .content-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.75rem); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.035em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .steps, ul { margin-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  p { color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .mt-2 { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .mt-4 { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .mt-6 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .mt-8 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .related { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .related p { line-height: 2; }
  .btn { text-decoration: none; }
  .converter label { display: block; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .converter textarea {
    width: 100%; padding: 0.9rem; border-radius: 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text); font: inherit; resize: vertical;
  }
  .converter-controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; }
  .converter-controls label { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .converter-controls input[type="range"] { flex: 1; min-width: 160px; }
  .bionic-output {
    padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg); line-height: 1.85; font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted); min-height: 6rem;
  }
  .bionic-output strong { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
